From 1732d8e8c415b7455a709dca666b42cde4586b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ry <ry@Mac.eau.wi.charter.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:07:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Nebulos seam: NebulosBridge, screen layouts, embedding
 init, UI hooks (RECONSTRUCTED)

Recreated from the decompiled Release 15 classes (me.magnum.melonds.nebulos.*, EmulatorActivity & friends):
- nebulos/NebulosBridge (Host callbacks notice/error/ready/loading/onKey/onMotion/onMenuRequested, queued until a host
  registers, active flag, screenLayout flow), NebulosScreenLayout(s) (NEBULOS pip / SINGLE / STACKED), RomUris (file: URIs)
- MelonDSApplication: no longer @HiltAndroidApp; companion loadNativeLib() + initializeForEmbedding(app) + EmbeddingEntryPoint
- WatermelonDSFileProvider (host re-declares the provider authority)
- EmulatorActivity: nebulosMode (intent extra "nebulos"), nebulosClose(), toasts/errors/loading to the bridge, key/motion/back
  routed to the host, FPS/loading views removed, pause menu & RA modals suppressed
- EmulatorViewModel/RuntimeLayoutView: Nebulos layout applied, soft controls hidden; settings: soft input always invisible
- EmulatorLaunchValidatorDelegate: dialogs become bridge errors; toasts in repositories become bridge notices
GUESSES: notice() long duration (5000 ms vs 2500 ms), nebulosClose() = closeEmulatorActivity() on the UI thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
